{"answerText":"**No—if the room is an assembly-purpose space that is accessory to the apartment building’s principal occupancy, it need not be classified as Group A-3.** A 900-net-square-foot room arranged with tables and chairs has an Assembly “unconcentrated (tables and chairs)” occupant load of 900 ÷ 15 = **60 occupants**. Because that is fewer than 75, BC 303.1.3 classifies an accessory assembly room as Group B or as part of the occupancy it serves; it nevertheless permits plumbing fixtures for that room to be calculated under the Assembly requirements. (BC §§ 1004.1.3, 303.1.3.)

The residents-only restriction does not by itself establish the required legal accessory relationship, and tables and chairs alone do not establish the room’s complete intended function. BC 303.4 covers assembly uses intended for worship, recreation, amusement, and other assembly uses not otherwise classified in Group A; classification must follow the actual intended use. If the room will be used for different purposes at different times, it must comply with the requirements applicable to each purpose. (BC §§ 303.4, 302.1.)

The separate under-75 rule in BC 303.1.2 applies to a **building or nonaccessory tenant space** used for assembly purposes; the supplied facts do not establish that this room is a nonaccessory tenant space. Confirmation of the room’s actual programmed uses and its accessory relationship to the principal occupancy is needed for final classification reliance.","supportedPoints":[{"heading":"Accessory assembly space below 75 occupants","explanation":"A room or space used for assembly purposes, with an occupant load of fewer than 75 persons, and accessory to another occupancy must be classified as Group B or as part of that occupancy. Plumbing fixtures for that room or space may be calculated under the Assembly-occupancy requirements.","sectionID":"132","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:132-4"]},{"heading":"Tables-and-chairs occupant-load factor","explanation":"Table 1004.1.3 assigns an occupant-load factor of 15 net square feet per occupant to Assembly space without fixed seats that is unconcentrated and arranged with tables and chairs.","sectionID":"2152","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:2152-2"]},{"heading":"A-3 scope depends on intended assembly use","explanation":"Group A-3 includes assembly uses intended for worship, recreation, amusement, and other assembly uses not classified elsewhere in Group A. A room or space intended for different purposes at different times must comply with the requirements applicable to each purpose.","sectionID":"135","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:135-1"]},{"heading":"Occupancy classification and nonaccessory tenant-space rule","explanation":"Structures or portions of structures must be classified by occupancy. Separately, a building or nonaccessory tenant space used for assembly purposes with fewer than 75 occupants is classified as Group B, with an Assembly-fixture calculation permitted. That rule is expressly limited to a building or nonaccessory tenant space.","sectionID":"128","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:128-3"]},{"heading":"Under-75 rule for buildings and nonaccessory tenant spaces","explanation":"A building or nonaccessory tenant space used for assembly purposes with fewer than 75 occupants is classified as Group B; its plumbing fixtures may be calculated under Assembly requirements.","sectionID":"131","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:131-5"]}],"assumptions":[],"missingFacts":["Whether the room is legally accessory to the apartment building’s principal occupancy; resident-only use does not independently establish that relationship.","The room’s actual intended activities and all uses at different times, which determine whether it is used for assembly purposes and whether another occupancy classification applies."],"followUpQuestions":[],"evidenceLimitations":["The supplied enacted evidence establishes the under-75 accessory-assembly rule and the tables-and-chairs occupant-load factor, but does not define the complete intended program of this multipurpose room or establish its accessory status."],"additionalEvidenceNeeded":["The programmed uses, operating restrictions, and approved occupancy/classification records or plans sufficient to verify the room’s intended use and accessory relationship."],"supportingSourceUses":[],"citations":[{"sectionID":"132","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:132-4"],"relevance":"Establishes the classification rule for an accessory assembly room with fewer than 75 occupants."},{"sectionID":"2152","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:2152-2"],"relevance":"Establishes the 15-net-square-foot-per-occupant factor for unconcentrated Assembly space with tables and chairs."},{"sectionID":"135","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:135-1"],"relevance":"Establishes the stated scope of Group A-3 assembly uses."},{"sectionID":"128","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:128-3"],"relevance":"Establishes general occupancy classification and the requirement to address each intended purpose of a multipurpose room."},{"sectionID":"131","sourceIDs":["research-permitext_discovered-id:131-5"],"relevance":"Establishes the separately limited under-75 rule for buildings and nonaccessory tenant spaces."}]}
